  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "9f73b909-d7aa-4298-a4fb-1a3ea26a029f",
    "name": "Abios Case Study — Live API",
    "description": "Spring Boot live-esports API — exercise every public endpoint and probes.\n\n## Before you send requests\n1. Start the app: `bash ./scripts/run.sh` (default **classpath mock**, port **8080**) or Atlas: `bash ./scripts/run-atlas.sh` (same as `SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=atlas` + `run.sh`) with `ABIOS_API_KEY`.\n2. Optional full bash sweep (needs curl): `bash ./scripts/run-full-api-verification.sh`.\n\n## Mock vs live\n| Mode | How you know |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Classpath mock** | JSON includes `seriesId` **ser-1001**, player **pl-501**, team **team-1** (from `src/main/resources/abios-mock/series-live.json`). No upstream HTTP. |\n| **Atlas / file mock** | Different IDs; set collection variable `expectMockData` = `false` so optional fingerprint tests are skipped. |\n\n## Variables\n- `baseUrl` — e.g. `http://localhost:8080`\n- `expectMockData` — `true` when using default mock (default); `false` for real Atlas.\n- `testClientIp` — `X-Forwarded-For` hop for an isolated rate-limit bucket (RFC 5737 doc space).\n\n## Rate limits\nPer-IP Bucket4j. For 429 + `Retry-After`, run **Collection Runner** on *Live data* with delay 0 until over limit, or use folder *Rate limiting*.\n\n## Pagination\nAll three live endpoints support optional `skip` and `take` query params for client-side pagination over the in-memory snapshot. Omitting them returns the full list (backwards-compatible).\n\n**Shape:** `{ \"meta\": { fetchedAt, stale, degraded, count, total, skip, take, hasMore }, \"items\": [...] }`. Errors: RFC 7807 where applicable.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "2896116",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/2896116-9f73b909-d7aa-4298-a4fb-1a3ea26a029f?source=collection_link"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Live data",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /v1/series/live",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"JSON has meta and items\", () => {",
                  "    const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(j).to.have.property(\"meta\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j).to.have.property(\"items\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.meta).to.have.property(\"fetchedAt\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.meta).to.have.property(\"stale\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.meta).to.have.property(\"degraded\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.meta).to.have.property(\"count\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.meta).to.have.property(\"total\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.meta).to.have.property(\"skip\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.meta).to.have.property(\"take\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.meta).to.have.property(\"hasMore\");",
                  "    pm.expect(j.meta.count).to.eql(j.items.length);",
                  "    pm.expect(j.meta.total).to.be.at.least(j.meta.count);",
                  "});",
                  "if (pm.collectionVariables.get(\"expectMockData\") === \"true\") {",
                  "    pm.test(\"Classpath mock fingerprint (series ser-1001)\", () => {",
                  "        const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "        const ids = j.items.map(i => i.seriesId);",
                  "        pm.expect(ids).to.include(\"ser-1001\");",
                  "    });",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "packages": {},
                "requests": {}
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/series/live",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "series",
                "live"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "skip",
                  "value": "0",
                  "description": "Items to skip (0-based offset). Omit to return all.",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "take",
                  "value": "10",
                  "description": "Max items to return. Omit or set to 0 to return all.",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Aggregated live series list from cached upstream snapshot. Supports optional `skip`/`take` for client-side pagination."
          },
          "response": []
        },
